From: SP11 Camera Parity <sp11-camera-parity@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: correct SP11 IFE1 DAL start prefix

The exact installed Windows qccamisp generation selector is now closed on
the same SP11: IFE1 index 1 is below the live threshold 2 and therefore
selects RVA 0x1be80 followed by the no-op RVA 0x1c0e0.

Retain the separately proven Windows-live TOP IRQ masks and BUS mask1 used
by the bounded Linux observer, but replace the wrong-generation DAL writes
with the active SP11 callback sequence: TOP core_cfg_0=7, core_cfg_1=0x10,
BUS mask0=0xdc000000 and BUS CGC override=0x1ff. The steady-state Windows
BUS mask0 contract 0xd0000000 remains a distinct value and is unchanged.

No sensor, CSID, RT-CDM, CSIPHY, DT, BUS-client or clock programming is
changed.

Signed-off-by: SP11 Camera Parity <sp11-camera-parity@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-680.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-680.c
@@ -155 +155,7 @@
-#define VFE680_X1E_DAL_START_TOP_ZERO  0x00000024
+#define VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_CORE_CFG0   0x00000024
+#define VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_CORE_CFG1   0x00000028
+#define VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_BUS_CGC_OVD 0x00000c08
+#define VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_CORE_CFG0_VALUE 0x00000007
+#define VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_CORE_CFG1_VALUE 0x00000010
+#define VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_BUS_MASK0   0xdc000000
+#define VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_BUS_CGC_OVD_VALUE 0x000001ff
@@ -1009 +1015,5 @@
-	/* Exact same-machine Windows VFE680 DAL_ife_start first-start prefix. */
+	/*
+	 * Retain the separately proven Windows-live IRQ visibility masks. They are
+	 * not owned by the active SP11 IFE1 DAL callback, whose generation selector
+	 * is now proven to be zero.
+	 */
@@ -1013,2 +1022,0 @@
-	writel_relaxed(VFE680_X1E_WINDOWS_BUS_MASK0,
-		       vfe->base + VFE_BUS_IRQn_MASK(vfe, 0));
@@ -1016 +1024,10 @@
-	writel_relaxed(0, vfe->base + VFE680_X1E_DAL_START_TOP_ZERO);
+
+	/* Exact active SP11 IFE1 callback RVA 0x1be80 write order. */
+	writel_relaxed(VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_CORE_CFG0_VALUE,
+		       vfe->base + VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_CORE_CFG0);
+	writel_relaxed(VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_CORE_CFG1_VALUE,
+		       vfe->base + VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_CORE_CFG1);
+	writel_relaxed(VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_BUS_MASK0,
+		       vfe->base + VFE_BUS_IRQn_MASK(vfe, 0));
+	writel_relaxed(VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_BUS_CGC_OVD_VALUE,
+		       vfe->base + VFE680_X1E_SP11_DAL_BUS_CGC_OVD);
